<title>USA: Sulzer pacemaker gets U.S. FDA approval.</title>
<headline>Sulzer pacemaker gets U.S. FDA approval.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON, Va. 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sulzer Medica, an operating group of Sulzer AG, said on Friday it received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market a dual-chamber rate-responsive pacemaker.</p>
<p>The so-called Momentum DR pacemaker, developed by Sulzer's cardiac arrhythmia management business, included an option which provided graphic or numeric depictions of key cardiac data, the company said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
